<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n100763" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνοδοντίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνόδους</span>) a
		large kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tunny</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.312b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> a fish of
			the Nile, Diph.Siph.ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.356f
			</span></i>: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνοδοντῖτις</span></b> 
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, ἡ, <i>a stone found in
				its head</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				37.182
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
